# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Only VITE_-prefixed values reach the browser
# (SPEC §10).
#
# ── Two backends, until Phase F ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# P9 moved identity, decks, cards and reviews to Cognito + API Gateway + RDS.
# /progress and card generation still read Supabase, because Phase B rewrites
# generation anyway and porting the progress aggregate is Phase F's work — doing
# either now would mean building it twice. See docs/plans/P9-aws-slice.md.
# So BOTH sets below are required to boot.


# ── AWS (P9) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three come from `cdk deploy` outputs. None is a secret: a pool id and a
# public app client id are in every browser bundle that talks to Cognito, by
# design, and the API endpoint is useless without a valid token.

# The ApiUrl output of SynapseDeck-Api-dev.
VITE_API_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxx.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com

# The UserPoolId and UserPoolClientId outputs of SynapseDeck-Auth-dev.
VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=us-east-1_xxxxxxxxx
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# There is NO app client secret, and there must never be one here. A browser SPA
# cannot hold a secret — shipping it in a bundle is publishing it — so the client
# is created with `generateSecret: false` (ADR 0007, infra/lib/auth-stack.ts).


# ── Supabase (until Phase F) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Values come from Supabase -> Settings -> API Keys.
#
# This project uses Supabase's modern key system (sb_publishable_… / sb_secret_…),
# not the legacy anon/service_role JWTs — those are deprecated at the end of 2026.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# The PUBLISHABLE key. Safe to ship to the browser: it carries no privileges of its
# own, and every request still runs as the `anon` or `authenticated` Postgres role
# under RLS.
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# NOT HERE, EVER: the secret key (sb_secret_…). It maps to `service_role`, which
# holds BYPASSRLS — one line of it in a client bundle exposes every user's data to
# anyone who reads your JavaScript. src/lib/env-schema.ts refuses to start if it
# finds one — that file holds the check; env.ts only applies it.
# v1 does not use a secret key at all; the Edge Function acts as the calling user.

# The generation provider key is likewise not set here. It lives only as an Edge
# Function secret, so it never reaches the client:
#   supabase secrets set GROQ_API_KEY=...



# ── AWS (P8 onward) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here is a client secret and nothing here reaches the browser in P8 —
# the frontend does not talk to AWS until P9. These are for CDK, locally.
#
# Credentials are NOT here and never are: the CLI reads ~/.aws/credentials, and
# CI assumes a role via GitHub OIDC with no stored key at all (ADR/D8).

# Budget and alarm notifications. Passed to CDK as -c alertEmail=… or read from
# here. Deliberately not committed with a real value: a personal address in a
# public repo is a spam magnet.
ALERT_EMAIL=you@example.com
